From a913dea5d2710df53c11a83222fcce761ebb101c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davide Depau <davide@depau.eu>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:12:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] elanmoc2: add driver for ELAN match-on-chip
 0c00/0c4c/0c5e/0c7c/0c90

Squash of libfprint MR !330 (Depau/libfprint elanmoc2, head 11f0316d),
rebased onto 6f9479c3 for Omarchy's libfprint-git pin.

Changed from the MR head while rebasing:
- The core changes to fp-device.c and fpi-device.c are left out: they
  change delete and STORAGE behaviour for every driver and fail
  libfprint's own fpi-device unit test. The driver sets
  FP_DEVICE_FEATURE_STORAGE itself instead.
- The recorded test (tests/elanmoc2) is left out: it asserts list and
  delete, which the MR head removed from the driver, so it fails on the
  MR as published.
- 0c5e, 0c7c and 0c90 leave the unsupported allowlist with 0c00 and
  0c4c, and data/autosuspend.hwdb is regenerated with
  fprint-list-udev-hwdb.
